ions\\n\\n1. **Establish triage rotation** — With 211 untriaged issues, implement a weekly triage rotation among maintainers to classify and label incoming issues. Set a team goal to keep untriaged under 20.\\n\\n2. **Community PR review sprint** — Dedicate time to review the 5 outstanding community PRs, especially #6449 (1,207 days old) and #7094 (713 days old). Either merge, request changes, or close with explanation.\\n\\n3. **Close stale questions with guidance** — Many unanswered questions from 2017-2020 may no longer be relevant. Review and close with pointers to updated documentation or suggest reopening if still applicable.\\n\\n4. **Address P0 issue #5805** — The MKLImports PDB issue has been open for nearly 5 years. Either resolve it or downgrade priority if it's no longer critical.\\n\\n5. **Automate \\\"awaiting user input\\\" cleanup** — Consider a bot that automatically closes issues labeled \\\"Awaiting User Input\\\" with no response after 60-90 days.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🔍 Correlation Insights\\n\\n- **High untriaged count + many old unanswered questions** suggests a maintainer bandwidth issue or triage process gap. The project may benefit from additional maintainers or community triage volunteers.\\n\\n- **5 community PRs with zero reviews (some >1000 days old)** indicates a critical community engagement problem. This can discourage future contributions and harm the project's reputation.\\n\\n- **100% CI success rate but low PR merge activity** — CI is healthy, but low merge velocity (0 PRs merged in 7 days) may indicate decision paralysis or lack of active development.\\n\\n- **Very old P0 and security issues** — Issues labeled P0 and Security remaining open for years suggests either mislabeling or insufficient prioritization of critical work.\\n\\n- **Low activity across all metrics (0 issues opened/closed, 0 PRs merged in 7 days)** — May indicate the repository is in maintenance mode or experiencing low maintainer bandwidth.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<sub>🤖 Gen